    'Labels fans use to identify themselves and the groups they build with.'                                                                                               => '',
    'Names for the individual elements you actually snap together.'                                                                                                        => '',
    'Names for set lines, exclusives, and what happens when a set retires.'                                                                                                => '',
    'Vocabulary for how AFOLs actually put bricks together.'                                                                                                               => '',
    'Vocabulary that pops up on resale sites and trade forums.'                                                                                                            => '',
    'Apps, databases and acronyms from around the LEGO ecosystem.'                                                                                                         => '',
    'An adult LEGO enthusiast, usually 18+, who actively follows the hobby.'                                                                                               => '',
    'A teenage LEGO fan, usually 13–17. The bridge between KFOL and AFOL.'                                                                                                 => '',
    'A child LEGO fan, the original target audience for most retail sets.'                                                                                                 => '',
    'An adult female LEGO fan. Used when distinguishing the demographic; otherwise AFOL covers everyone.'                                                                  => '',
    'A community of AFOLs that meets locally or online to build and share the hobby.'                                                                                      => '',
    'A LUG officially recognized by The LEGO Group, eligible for support like exclusive sets for events.'                                                                  => '',
    'The official channel through which TLG communicates with recognized LUGs and ambassadors worldwide.'                                                                  => '',
    'The Danish company that designs and manufactures LEGO products.'                                                                                                      => '',
    'The classic rectangular element with studs on top. The building block of every LEGO set (e.g. 2x4, 1x2).'                                                             => '',
    'A flat element one third of a brick’s height. Three stacked plates equal the height of one brick.'                                                                    => '',
    'A flat element with no studs on top, used for smooth surfaces, floors, and details.'                                                                                  => '',
    'The cylindrical bump on top of a brick or plate that allows pieces to snap together.'                                                                                 => '',
    'An angled element used for roofs, ramps and other non-flat surfaces.'                                                                                                 => '',
    'A tiny 1x1 sloped piece named for its wedge shape; a workhorse for greebling and small details.'                                                                      => '',
    'A plate with a single centered stud, used to offset other parts by half a stud.'                                                                                      => '',
    'A large thin plate that serves as the foundation for a build. Not stackable like regular plates.'                                                                     => '',
    'A small set (usually under 100 pieces) sold in a sealed plastic bag instead of a box. Often promotional.'                                                             => '',
    'A Star Wars line of large, display-focused sets aimed at adult collectors, often with high piece counts.'                                                             => '',
    'A premium set distributed mainly via LEGO.com and brand stores rather than mass-market retailers.'                                                                    => '',
    'A small bonus set given free with qualifying orders, typically time-limited and used to drive sales.'                                                                 => '',
    'LEGO’s free loyalty program: earn points on purchases, redeem for sets, GWPs, or experiences.'                                                                        => '',
    'An adult-oriented line of stackable city buildings (32x32 stud footprint) that connect side by side.'                                                                 => '',
    'A mini-build polybag bundled with a collectible LEGO magazine at newsstands and kiosks.'                                                                              => '',
    'A set sold only through official LEGO channels (LEGO.com, brand stores) and not via mass retailers.'                                                                  => '',
    'A set officially out of production. Stock dries up and aftermarket prices tend to climb.'                                                                             => '',
    'A set scheduled for retirement. Once EOL is reached, no more units will be produced.'                                                                                 => '',
    'A small set distributed as a giveaway, contest prize, or partnership bonus rather than retail sale.'                                                                  => '',
    'A model designed and built from scratch by a fan, not based on any official LEGO set.'                                                                                => '',
    'A family of techniques that orient studs sideways or downward, used for smooth surfaces and unusual angles.'                                                          => '',
    'A pre-assembled element (like a pre-printed wall section) replacing what builders would rather construct themselves. Generally seen as a negative.'                   => '',
    'A large, single-mold rock element. Disliked because it removes the chance to build rocks from smaller parts.'                                                         => '',
    'Adding small decorative parts (pipes, antennas, gears) to make a surface look busy and technical. Popular on spaceships.'                                             => '',
    'Building at a scale much smaller than minifigure scale, e.g. a whole castle that fits in your palm.'                                                                  => '',
    'The default scale (roughly 1:42) where models are sized for minifigures to interact with.'                                                                            => '',
    'A connection that works but violates LEGO’s internal design rules (e.g. stressing a part). Common in fan MOCs, rare in official sets.'                                => '',
    'The largest online marketplace for LEGO parts, minifigures, and sets, also home to the Stud.io builder.'                                                              => '',
    'A set still factory-sealed in its original box, in pristine condition. Commands the highest resale prices.'                                                           => '',
    'A set that has never been opened. Often used interchangeably with MISB.'                                                                                              => '',
    'A complete set with original box, but the seal may be broken. Lower value than MISB/NISB.'                                                                            => '',
    'Official LEGO stores (LEGO.com and physical brand stores). The primary source for exclusives and GWPs.'                                                               => '',
    'The price a set commands on the secondary market after retiring from retail. Often used to track sets as investments.'                                                => '',
    'A set bought primarily because it’s expected to grow in value after retirement, rather than to build.'                                                                => '',
    'An open standard and library of part files for digital LEGO models. The foundation of most third-party CAD tools.'                                                    => '',
    'A free LEGO CAD program from BrickLink with rendering, building instructions and a parts-ordering flow.'                                                              => '',
    'LEGO’s official (now discontinued) CAD program. Replaced in the community by Stud.io.'                                                                                => '',
    'A community database of sets, parts, and minifigures, with alternate-build instructions for parts you already own.'                                                   => '',
    'A long-running set database with reviews, news, prices, and collection-tracking tools for AFOLs.'                                                                     => '',
    'A competing brick brand (e.g. COBI, Mega Construx) producing LEGO-compatible elements. Generally not considered "LEGO".'                                              => '',
